- 当 $a=0, b \neq 0$ 时, $\displaystyle\int \frac{\mathrm{d} x}{a^2 \sin ^2 x+b^2 \cos ^2 x}\\=\frac{1}{b^2} \int \frac{\mathrm{d} x}{\cos ^2 x}\\=\frac{1}{b^2} \tan x+C$;

- 当 $a \neq 0, b=0$ 时, $\displaystyle\int \frac{\mathrm{d} x}{a^2 \sin ^2 x+b^2 \cos ^2 x}\\=\frac{1}{a^2} \int \frac{\mathrm{d} x}{\sin ^2 x}\\=-\frac{1}{a^2} \cot x+C$;

- 当 $a \neq 0, b \neq 0$ 时, $\displaystyle\int \frac{\mathrm{d} x}{a^2 \sin ^2 x+b^2 \cos ^2 x} \\ =\int \frac{\sec ^2 x}{b^2+(a \tan x)^2} \mathrm{d} x \\ =\frac{1}{a} \int \frac{\mathrm{d}(a \tan x)}{b^2+(a \tan x)^2}\\=\frac{1}{a b} \arctan \frac{a \tan x}{b}+C$
